  m_Name: TannerWellington
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ResumeData
  applicantName: Tanner Wellington
  body: '<b>TANNER WELLINGTON</b>

    Applying for: Vice President of Everything


    <b>EXPERIENCE</b>

    {title}

    {dates}


    <b>EDUCATION</b>

    {edu}


    <b>SKILLS</b>

    {skill_golf},
    {skill_lead}


    <b>REFERENCES</b>

    {ref}'
  claims:
  - id: title
    text: Junior Vice Assistant to the CEO (my uncle)
    isSuspicious: 1
    category: 2
    designerNote: No real management experience breaks rule 10.
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: What did you do as Junior Vice Assistant?
      answer: I {t_clubs}. And I {t_ideas}.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases:
      - id: t_clubs
        text: carried my uncle's golf clubs
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: Very heavy clubs. That's leadership.
        callOutDemeanor: 1
      - id: t_ideas
        text: had many great ideas
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: Like a pool in the meeting room. Uncle said no. For now.
        callOutDemeanor: 1
    goodQuestion:
      question: Working closely with the CEO is good experience.
      answer: I'm very close to him. At Thanksgiving I sit right next to him.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases: []
  - id: dates
    text: Summer 2025 (8 weeks)
    isSuspicious: 1
    category: 1
    designerNote: 
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: You've only worked for eight weeks?
      answer: Eight very intense weeks. And I only took {w_breaks}.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases:
      - id: w_breaks
        text: six weeks of vacation
        isContradiction: 1
        callOutResponse: Okay, two weeks of work. But they were VERY intense weeks.
          I had a headache once.
        callOutDemeanor: 3
    goodQuestion:
      question: Short but sweet.
      answer: Exactly. Quality over quantity. Uncle says that about me a lot.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases: []
  - id: edu
    text: Business degree (purchased)
    isSuspicious: 1
    category: 0
    designerNote: 
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: Your degree says '(purchased)'.
      answer: All degrees are purchased. That's how {e_college}.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases:
      - id: e_college
        text: college works
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: My uncle bought me a degree and a building. The building
          has my name on it.
        callOutDemeanor: 1
    goodQuestion:
      question: A business degree. Nice.
      answer: It's framed in gold. Real gold. The degree itself is mostly paper.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases: []
  - id: skill_golf
    text: 'Golf (handicap: 40)'
    isSuspicious: 0
    category: 4
    designerNote: 
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: Is golf really a job skill?
      answer: It's THE skill. All the big deals happen on the golf course. I've made
        {g_deals}.
      demeanor: 0
      phrases:
      - id: g_deals
        text: zero deals
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: Zero so far. But I've had a lot of nice lunches.
        callOutDemeanor: 0
    goodQuestion:
      question: Golf is good for networking.
      answer: Very good. I once lost a ball in a pond and a CEO helped me find it.
        We're best friends now.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases: []
  - id: skill_lead
    text: Leadership (natural)
    isSuspicious: 0
    category: 4
    designerNote: 
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: How have you shown leadership?
      answer: I once led my friends to a pizza place. Everyone followed me. {l_lost}.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases:
      - id: l_lost
        text: We got lost for three hours
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: But we were together. That's leadership.
        callOutDemeanor: 1
    goodQuestion:
      question: Natural leadership. Love it.
      answer: Thank you. People say I was born to lead. My uncle says it. He's people.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases: []
  - id: ref
    text: Uncle Richard (CEO of Synergix)
    isSuspicious: 1
    category: 5
    designerNote: Family reference breaks rule 3.
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: Your reference is the CEO. Your uncle.
      answer: Is that a problem? He said {u_problem}.
      demeanor: 5
      phrases:
      - id: u_problem
        text: it wouldn't be a problem
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: He also said you'd be 'very understanding'. Wink. He told
          me to say wink.
        callOutDemeanor: 5
    goodQuestion:
      question: The CEO recommends you. Hard to argue with that.
      answer: Exactly. Uncle Richard says I'm the future of this company. He said
        it at a wedding. He was very tired.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases: []
  referenceLetter: 'To whom it may concern,


    My nephew Tanner is {rl_future}
    of this company. I say this as his {rl_family}, but also as a CEO.


